<header class="phead"><div class="wrap"><h1>Chandler<span class="h1-sub">Procurement</span></h1><p>Chandler runs the part of procurement that is mostly chasing: getting quotes back from vendors who are slow to respond, then making sure the price on the invoice matches the price that was agreed.</p></div></header><section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="split"><div><h2>How Chandler does the work.</h2><p class="intro">Runs RFQ to PO with multi-vendor negotiation across email, SMS and voice, then holds suppliers to the pricing schedule they agreed to.</p><ol class="runbook"><li><span class="n">01</span><div><h4>Issues the RFQ to everyone at once</h4><p>The same specification goes to every qualified vendor simultaneously, in whichever channel that vendor actually answers: email for some, SMS for others, and a phone call for the ones who never read either.</p></div></li><li><span class="n">02</span><div><h4>Chases the non-responders</h4><p>Most of the elapsed time in an RFQ is waiting. Chandler follows up on a schedule, escalates to a second contact when the first goes quiet, and reports which vendors are habitually slow so the panel can be pruned.</p></div></li><li><span class="n">03</span><div><h4>Normalizes the responses</h4><p>Quotes arrive in different units, currencies, incoterms and payment terms. Chandler restates them on one basis so the comparison is real, and flags where a headline price hides a freight or minimum-order difference.</p></div></li><li><span class="n">04</span><div><h4>Recommends the award, with the math</h4><p>A ranked recommendation showing landed cost, lead time, terms and past performance, with the arithmetic shown, so the buyer can disagree with a number rather than a conclusion.</p></div></li><li><span class="n">05</span><div><h4>Holds the price after the handshake</h4><p>The agreed schedule is extracted from the contract and monitored. When an invoice arrives above the agreed rate, or a rate rises before its review date, Chandler flags it against the clause it breaches.</p></div></li></ol></div><aside><div class="panel"><p class="h">Connects to</p><ul><li>SAP HANA</li><li>NetSuite</li><li>Dynamics 365</li><li>Email</li><li>SMS</li><li>Voice</li></ul></div><div class="panel"><p class="h">What you get back</p><ul><li>Normalized quote comparison</li><li>Ranked award recommendation with workings</li><li>Extracted contract terms and review dates</li><li>Price variance alerts against schedule</li></ul></div><div class="panel"><p class="h">Deployed in</p><ul><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/industries/food-and-beverage' ) ); ?>">Food &amp; beverage</a></li><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/industries/construction' ) ); ?>">Construction</a></li><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/industries/manufacturing' ) ); ?>">Manufacturing</a></li><li><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/industries/logistics-and-supply-chain' ) ); ?>">Logistics &amp; supply chain</a></li></ul></div></aside></div><p class="gate"><strong>Where Chandler stops.</strong> Chandler negotiates and recommends. It does not commit spend. The award and the purchase order are released by a person.</p></div></section><section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="bespoke"><h3>Your agents are built around your organization.</h3><p>The way you price, route, approve and escalate is years of accumulated judgment, and it's a real advantage. It belongs to you and it stays with you, we're not asking you to hand over your playbook or fit yourself into someone else's template. We start from how your business already works, encode that logic into agents built for your environment, and leave you with an operation that runs faster with exactly the things that make you good at it still intact.</p></div><p class="more"><a href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/work' ) ); ?>">See all six agents →</a></p></div></section><section class="cta"><div class="wrap"><h2>Bring us one workflow.</h2><p>Thirty minutes, no deck. Pick the process that costs you most in people, errors or delay, and we'll pressure-test whether an agent is genuinely the right answer for it.</p><ul class="cta-list"><li>An honest read on whether that workflow is a good agent candidate</li><li>What the first deployment would involve, and roughly what it costs</li><li>An honest answer if the sequencing is wrong and you should fix something else first</li></ul><a class="btn btn-lg" href="<?php echo esc_url( home_url( '/contact' ) ); ?>">Book a discovery call</a></div></section>
